<!doctype html>
<!-- ABOUTME: The TV's offline setup page: join the setup hotspot from a phone, then pick Wi-Fi. -->
<!-- ABOUTME: shulportal-refresh fills in the hotspot name and an inline SVG Wi-Fi join code. -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>ShulPortal setup</title>
<style>
  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0b1f3a; color: #fff; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: none; }
  main { height: 100%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 6vw; padding: 0 6vw; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .qr { background: #fff; padding: 1.5vw; border-radius: 1vw; width: 28vw; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .qr svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  h1 { font-size: 4.5vw; margin: 0 0 1vw; font-weight: 600; }
  .ssid { font-size: 3.6vw; font-weight: 700; color: #e3b341; margin: 0 0 3vw; white-space: nowrap; }
  p { font-size: 2.6vw; line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; max-width: 45vw; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <div class="qr">{{QR}}</div>
  <div>
    <h1>Connect your phone to Wi-Fi</h1>
    <p class="ssid">{{SSID}}</p>
    <p>Then pick the shul's Wi-Fi on the page that opens and enter its password.</p>
  </div>
</main>
</body>
</html>
